- op: discuss  # 2160
  at: '2026-04-24T02:00:25Z'  # 2160
  by: agent  # 2160
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2160
  clock: 4  # 2160
  nonce: '2160'  # 2160
  message: "Catalog adds reverted in PR3 of stop-stripping plan. The WI-jihuj fix was the wrong layer — the catalog is for true I/O primitives, not arbitrary third-party wrappers. The structural answer (IoChain.dst_tier from PR2) lets verify-claims reason about tier-3 destinations as 'may make network calls' without per-library catalog growth. Awaits-bakeoff-validation tag retained: bakeoff should confirm this revert doesn't regress real net_send detection on diverse repos."  # 2160
